WEBVTT

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.600
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.930
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.140
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:19.670
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:29.920
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.350
Go! Go!

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:36.730
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.630
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.000
Always in the good days in my life!

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:50.000
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.380
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.820
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.950
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.430
is a memory I carry with me.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.790
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.160
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.560
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.470
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.130
What are you doing, May?

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.340
This isn't safe, so I thought I'd strengthen it.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.950
To get ready for the typhoon?

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.440
Yes! Exactly!

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.520
Well, even so...

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.000
Don't you think you're sort of overdoing it?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.560
Roll, roll, roll...

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.260
Shoo! Shoo!

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.430
You really think so?

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:07.530
Oh, definitely. You're definitely overdoing this!

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.390
Oh, my, my, my. Not at all.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.730
Look, even Shikishima's doing it.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.570
See?

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.490
Now those are shutters!

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.240
Shikishima doesn't count!

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.240
If Mr. Typhoon is taking the trouble to visit us, the least we can do is greet him properly.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.100
Like they say, "Be prepared and you'll be happy!"

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.250
Okay, Mr. Typhoon!

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.580
Come and get us any time and anywhere you want to!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.000
So, how do you plan on getting back into the room, Mami?

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.530
But Kasumi, we have to be prepared for something bad happening.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.680
I know. I know that.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:48.290
But still...

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:49.480
Kasumi!

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.120
MAY IS ABSOLUTELY RIGHT!

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.160
This typhoon looks like it'll be a big one!

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.570
We can't be too cautious about it!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.750
Kazuya always takes May's side.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:05.830
Kasumi?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:06.830
Right?

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.580
All right, all right. I'll leave it to you.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.610
Right!

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:20.540
MAY!

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.590
Saotome!

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.600
SAOTOME!

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.190
Saotome! Ya ain't hurt, are ya?!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.620
Uh... No...

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:35.740
Thank God!

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.860
Out of the way! Out of my way, Saotome!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:42.870
Who cares about you?! My silky, milky, lovely May!

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.120
I MUST SAVE MY BELOVED MAY!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.010
What are they doing?

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.050
Thank you so much, Kazuya.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.530
And you, May. You shouldn't push yourself.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.670
Right. Sorry.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.310
And thank you very much, Kasumi!

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.720
What's up with that thing, anyway?!

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.570
First of all, that's no place for a ladder!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.800
For placing my beloved May in danger,

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.580
I, Kotaro Nanbara, will never forgive you, heartless ladder!

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:32.400
FOR THAT, YOU MUST DIE!

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.080
Put a cork in it!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.880
You're one to talk about being heartless.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.490
What did you say?!

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:42.590
What a pain. Does he hafta yell all the time?

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:47.600
I was going to take that ladder down after I moved in.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.150
Things just kept me from doing it.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.100
WHAT SORT OF THINGS?!

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.690
This sort of thing and that sort of thing, you mean?!

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.940
And you'd hide them from me, your dearest of friends?!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.470
You've got some nerve!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.720
YOU'D BETTER TELL ME EVERYTHING NOW, SAOTOME!

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.600
Oh, my, my, my...

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.480
I wanna hear, too!

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.620
This is far more interesting than the typhoon!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.930
I'll cry! I'LL CRY!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.450
Um, well...

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:18.020
Don't be so excited. It's not that big a deal.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.910
That's for us to decide!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.920
Go on! Go on! Tell us now, SAOTOME!

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.140
Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.070
Who cares about the typhoon now?!

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.680
I'll cry! I swear, I'LL CRY!

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.030
Even if you give me those looks...

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.620
Kazuya, I want to hear about it, too.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.120
Y-You, too, May?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.100
Yes!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.580
I want to know more about you and Kasumi.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.960
Please tell me!

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.240
<i>Will you tell them?</i>

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.070
Oh, boy... Well...

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:53.060
The ladder is a much shorter way for Kasumi to take, than if she walks around and uses the stairs.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.780
Yeah, we know that already!

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.500
Are there any other reasons?! TELL US!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.090
Um... Let's see...

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.690
She uses it to bring me food and to wake me up in the morning.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:10.340
All sorts of fun things, right?

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.570
Yeah, well...

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:14.830
Huh?

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.720
Your story bored us to death.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.770
Well, I told you not to expect too much from it.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:26.110
YES! I was a stupid idiot to have expected a good story from you!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.480
Just what did you want to hear?!

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.140
Kazuya?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.870
Yes? Oh!

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.450
The landlady?!

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.370
Kazuya...

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:42.380
This takes me back. I haven't crossed this in a long time.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.130
By the way, is Kasumi visiting you?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.590
Huh? She was just here, but...

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:52.090
Really? She always seems to be over here, so I thought...

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:58.470
Where could she have gone in the middle of a typhoon?

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:00.350
I'll go look for her.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.370
Sorry to trouble you.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:06.710
In return, you can pay the rent late.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.370
Um, thanks.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.120
Oh, my, my, my. Chigusa, really!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.350
Th-That was cool!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:18.200
"Like mother, like daughter" certainly applies in this case!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.160
There's much more to this ladder than I first anticipated.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.180
Boring...

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.640
Wait! I'll go with you!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.990
It's too dangerous, May. Stay here. I'll be back soon.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.760
Of course! Of course! Get going! And then...

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:37.890
VANISH FOREVER WITH THE LANDLADY'S RUDE, VIOLENT DAUGHTER!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.660
I'll go with you, too!

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.850
Whatever! And I'll stay here with my beloved May, and—

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.610
I'm going, too!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.320
May...

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.430
Kazuya!

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.470
May!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.350
Wait for me!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.420
Wait up!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.140
Kazuya!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.570
M-May!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.580
What is this, a cartoon?!

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.080
<i>Why did you tell them?</i>

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.090
<i>Because May asked you to?</i>

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.590
<i>Will you do anything that May asks you to do?</i>

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.480
Um, excuse me.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.100
Here.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.560
It's the same last name as mine, isn't it?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.150
You shouldn't read other peoples' mail!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.370
Would you cut it out?!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.370
Um, you forgot these.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.130
Th-Thanks...

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:14.320
Um, hi, I'm Saotome. I just moved into apartment 204.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.270
Nice to meet you.

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:18.020
Y-You, too...

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:18.980
See you.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.100
Clumsy...

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.560
Clumsy Saotome...

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.170
Kasumi!

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.590
Kazuya...

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.830
You're gonna catch a cold.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.320
Come on, let's go home.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.260
Come on.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.730
Look, Kasumi—

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.720
Clumsy...

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.370
Clumsy Saotome...

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:33.380
Did you see that fall he took off the swing and then that shot to his shins!

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.840
Just shut up!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:41.510
Saotome... You haven't called me that in a long time.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:50.520
Back when you called me that, you were so wild.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.290
Remember that time when I had the ladder up against the wall?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.350
H-Hold it! What are you doing—

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.480
S-Sorry...

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:24.680
Sorry for making you worry.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.590
Hey, no problem, no problem.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.870
Maybe that ladder isn't worth the trouble.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:32.900
Uh-uh.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.580
I like that ladder.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.140
So do I.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.430
Nice story. Nice story!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:50.280
That's a really nice story.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:51.780
In what way?!

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.350
Anyway, right now...

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.390
Let's hurry home!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.010
Right!

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:58.100
Ma-a-a-ay!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.590
<i>Mika!</i>

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:01.610
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:02.760
<i>Mika!</i>

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:05.110
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.880
<i>M-MIKA!</i>

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.920
Yama-ma-ma-ma....

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:10.120
<i>MIKA!</i>

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.780
Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes!

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.160
Oh, May.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:25.920
Wind speeds are gusting to 70 meters per second,

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.880
and the force level is still rising! Incredible!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:31.530
It's gonna blow this crappy apartment away!

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.890
The ladder!

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:41.610
It's too dangerous, May! Leave that dirty old ladder alone!

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:47.330
It can't blow away! This ladder...

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:50.330
Kazuya and Kasumi treasure this ladder!

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.350
Hit us with your best shot!

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:05.210
With this many of us on here, it won't blow away!

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.700
It may just break, instead.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.540
NEVER SAY DIE!

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.610
Yeah!

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:11.560
Master Nanbara...

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:12.720
What?!

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:16.340
There's some good in you yet.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:23.310
Of course I'd do this! I'm doing it all for May!

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.730
What?

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.680
Are you getting embarrassed?!

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:27.730
Shut up!

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:31.490
Never mind that! The brat!

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.370
Nice catch, Squiddy!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:50.880
GUTS!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.590
IT'LL TAKE MORE THAN THAT!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:54.090
IS THAT THE BEST YOU CAN DO?!

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.800
Would you quit yellin'?

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.270
THIS IS ALL SAOTOME'S FAULT!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:10.210
Sara! Nanbara! Mami!

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.280
Now it's all a question of attitude!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.770
Anyway, with just us on here...

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.780
Huh? We must be in the eye of the storm.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:32.980
Now's our chance!

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.110
Kasumi!

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:37.750
Jeez...

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.720
Right, right...

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:47.030
May, what are you doing up there?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.730
Oh! Kasumi!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:54.240
I was protecting your precious ladder!

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:56.990
Um, you see...

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:01.880
I overheard you and Kazuya talking before, so...

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.710
Y-You heard?

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:07.420
That's why... I want a ladder like this, too!

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.760
That's why I was protecting it!

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.760
May...

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:14.220
Thank you.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.640
Sorry to break the mood,

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:20.750
but the second half of the storm's starting!

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:25.340
May, can we do this together?

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:25.980
Sure!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.610
<i>I won't give up, either!</i>

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.200
Oh, my, my, my?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.110
May and Kasumi aren't here, are they?

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.710
Huh? Where'd they go?

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:52.180
By the way, Chigusa, that ladder seems to have quite a history.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:56.400
Oh, yes. It has an amazing origin.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:57.730
Oh? What is it?

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:03.590
Oh, my, my, my! You don't say!

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.380
I must hear it, too! I have to know now!

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.850
Hurry up and tell us!

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.230
Oh, my, my, my...

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.610
Um, thanks for the clothes.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.740
I'll return them after I've washed them.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:23.060
Oh, that's all right. Don't worry about it.

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.310
But...

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.000
May.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:26.740
Yes?

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.960
The ladder... You want it?

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.140
Yes!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.460
Did I say something funny?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:40.390
Sorry, sorry. But what are you gonna use it for?

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.540
Well, let's see...

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.510
To wake Kazuya up every morning.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:48.480
To bring Kazuya food every day.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:51.100
To go to the amusement park together,

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.250
and to go shopping together, and...

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:57.050
But you can do all that without the ladder, right?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:00.010
Yeah, I guess...

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:01.010
Look, May...

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:02.030
Yes?

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:07.560
It isn't the ladder you really want.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:12.460
Maybe what you really want

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:19.680
are the memories of all the things connected to it.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.300
Memories?

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.540
Well, for example,

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:28.210
the stuff Kazuya and I talked about in the park before.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:32.080
Oh, I see! Those are the memories I want!

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:34.690
I want to have so many of them!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:38.680
So many? May, you have so many already.

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:40.410
Huh? Do I really?

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:44.700
C'mon, even today will become a nice memory.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.330
Yeah! That's right!

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:51.670
Look, you remember all the stuff that's happened since you first came here, right?

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.320
Sure! Of course.

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:57.380
Those are all your memories, May.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:19:59.840
Those are memories?

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:04.980
Memories aren't the ladder or that sort of stuff.

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:08.780
They're what you've accomplished by doing your best.

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:10.910
Things you've done with other people.

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:16.350
The little things that pass you by that you hardly notice.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.110
Right!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:22.770
When I look at you, I can't believe you're a robot, May.

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:25.220
You act so human...

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:28.120
Huh? How so?

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.990
Well, anyway...

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.840
Tomorrow, I'm going to give everything my best!

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:36.300
Hey! You stole my catch-phrase!

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:45.780
<i>Today was a lot of trouble but, like Kasumi said, it's a nice memory now.</i>

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:49.830
<i>I hope I can make a lot more nice memories in days to come.</i>

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.640
<i>Tomorrow, I'm going to give everything my best!</i>

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:02.280
What's wrong, Sara? Aren't you hungry?

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:05.480
What about you, Master Nanbara? All you do is sigh.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:06.920
Yeah.

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:13.250
You don't suppose...

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:15.340
WE'RE LOVE SICK?!

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:22.870
WHO ARE YOU?!

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:24.420
Can it be...?!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:30.290
Who the hell are you?! HOW DARE YOU!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.770
T-TELL ME YOUR NAME!

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:37.510
Y-Y-YOU BARBARIAN!

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:43.720
L-L-Lemme go, you... y-y-y-you insolent...!

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:59.670
When I'm with you, I blush till my ears turn red.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:04.280
I wonder why that is...

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:10.480
When I'm alone with you I can never seem to do anything right.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:18.320
I become so tongue-tied i can't speak at all.

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:25.460
It's strange, don't you think? I think about it too much.

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:34.910
Is this love? I just can't accept that at all.

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:41.610
I can't be honest. I want so much to be.

00:22:41.610 --> 00:22:48.340
Someday, perhaps, you'll tell me

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:56.310
the true feelings that are in my heart.

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:00.870
Mami's popularity has been skyrocketing lately!

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:01.710
Oh, my, my, my!

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:03.950
Guys are just melting over that apron outfit!

00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:04.850
Oh, my, my, my!

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:06.350
They say they want to see you do more stuff.

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:07.300
Oh, my, my, MY!

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:08.880
But, in two episodes... the show's over.

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:09.030
Huh?!

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:09.500
Huh...!?
Huh?!

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:09.570
Oh, my, my, my...
Huh...!?

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:10.600
Oh, my, my, my...

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:12.970
"Besides That... I Believe You"
